# Tierra Rejada GSPro build: handoff notes (Oct 23, 2026, updated after the Mac shrub/OB/deep-rough session)

Real course: Tierra Rejada Golf Club, Moorpark CA (Bob Cupp, 1999). Built by James for GSPro with the free OPCD toolset. Status: **playable in GSPro** with satellite colours, 1,412 LiDAR trees, split-rail fence, stone wall on 3, range net. Cart paths built in data, not yet confirmed in Unity.

## Machines and locations
- **PC (Windows):** Unity 2018.2.8f1 (exact version the base project needs), GSPro, Greenkeeper 4.1.0.
  - Unity project: `C:\GSP\GSPBaseProject_v4_2025_12_02` (scene `TierraRejada.unity`, our files in `Assets\TierraRejada\`, editor tools in `Assets\Editor\`)
  - GSPro course folder: `C:\GSProV1\Core\GSP\Courses\TierraRejada\` (`TierraRejada.gspcrse`, `TierraRejada.GKD`, `coursedetails.txt`, `.gspcrse.csv`, scorecard jpgs, `TR.jpg` splash)
  - Greenkeeper: `C:\GSP\GreenKeeper\GreenKeeper.exe`
  - Git repo: `Documents\tierra-rejada` â†’ github.com/boshersjames/tierra-rejada
- **Mac:** repo copy `~/Tierra` (run `git pull` before committing). LiDAR work in `~/tierra-lidar` with Python venv `~/venv` (always run `~/venv/bin/python`, not `python3`).
  - `tierra_points.npz` (17.25 M points, 2018 USGS SoCal Wildfires B3 survey), `TierraRejada_satellite.jpg` (NAIP, 4096 px, 0.49 m/px)
  - Scripts (also in repo `lidar_scripts/`): `get_lidar.py`, `get_satellite.py`, `find_trees.py`, `find_brush.py`

## Coordinate frame (everything uses this)
- 2000 m square. SW corner EPSG:6340 (NAD83(2011) UTM 11N) = 328865.84 E, 3792716.77 N; centre 34.2707005, -118.848084.
- Unity x = metres east of SW corner, z = metres north, y = elevation âˆ’ 182 m.
- Heightmap `terrain/tierra_rejada_2049.raw`: 2049Ã—2049, 16-bit little-endian (Windows), rows = z, size 2000 Ã— 207 Ã— 2000.
- Convert Google Maps lat/long with pyproj EPSG:4326 â†’ EPSG:6340, then subtract the SW corner.

## Unity workflow that works
- GSP â†’ Add OPCD Meshes (FBX from `TierraRejada_fbx`), SetMeshMaterials v4, Lower Terrain Under Meshes (1 m), Build Course (scene TierraRejada; both "disable collider" boxes checked).
- **Materials:** theme `TierraRejada_sat` = v4_satellite with Terrain Satellite = `TierraRejada_satellite` (Max Size 4096), Terrain Size 2000, BUT Green / Fairway / Tee on **default** materials (the real ones under `Assets/Resources`, not the white placeholders in `SampleScenefbx`). Bunker = Sand Raked Dirt Lip Thin.
- Physics materials in `Assets/Resources/Physics`: GSPtimber, GSPleaves, GSPstone, GSPconcrete, GSPdeeprough, GSPrough, GSPsemirough, etc. Build fails/warns if colliders lack one.
- Rebuilding the course only replaces `.gspcrse`; GKD and other files stay.

## Our Unity editor tools (menu **Tierra**)
- `PlantLidarTrees.cs`: plants `trees/tierra_trees.csv` (1,412 trees within 150 m of play, LiDAR heights) from `Assets/Trees/Broadleaf` (Desktop SpeedTree only, skips "Mobile"); trunk colliders â†’ GSPtimber, canopy â†’ GSPleaves. Parent `LIDAR_TREES`.
- `BuildFences.cs`: one window with fences (`fences.csv`, split-rail 1.07 m, 3 runs), stone walls (`walls.csv`, hole 3 retaining wall, GSPstone), range nets (`nets.csv`, 19 m poles, 170 m, GSPleaves, transparency slider; real net looks darker, try ~0.5).
- `BuildCartPaths.cs`: `cartpaths.csv` from OpenStreetMap (25 golf cart paths, 8,655 m), 2.4 m concrete strips, GSPconcrete.
- `DrawArea.cs`: click points in Scene view to make Deep Rough / Rough / Semi Rough patches (draped, proper physics) or OB outlines; saves to `Assets/TierraRejada/areas/*.csv`. Not yet tested.

## Greenkeeper (GKD) lessons
- Unused tee slots must be `"Enabled": false` when Position is null, or GSPro shows "500 yds par 0".
- Save from Greenkeeper itself (it writes coursedetails.txt, .gspcrse.csv, scorecards). Altitude field is feet: 800.
- Splash must be .jpg in the course folder (phone photos need EXIF rotation; current TR.jpg may still be sideways, delete `image_altered*` cache after fixing).

## Course data
- Tee markers â†’ GSPro slots: Professional/Black â†’ Black, Championship/Grey â†’ **Green**, Tournament/Blue â†’ Blue, Players/White â†’ White, Forward/Gold â†’ **Yellow**, Red unused.
- Ratings: Black 73.5/135, Grey 70.9/129, Blue 68.7/124, White 66.4/118, Gold 64.3/111. Pars 5 3 4 5 4 4 3 4 5 / 4 3 5 4 3 4 5 3 4 (72). Men's SI 5 11 1 7 15 13 17 3 9 / 6 10 16 2 12 8 18 14 4.
- All tees confirmed by James except Blue/White/Gold on 6 and Gold on 5. Card runs ~3% long vs true distances (verified with Google Maps on hole 2). 10/28: BoJa now wants yardages to match the card where possible; they will photograph the full card (all colours) and pin any further-back boxes on 3, 18, 4, 12, 6 and 1. Biggest Black gaps: 3 (-28), 18 (-21), 4 and 12 (-20), 6 (-19), 1 (-15).
- Aim points set: 3 (driver line, 250 carry from 6,000-yd tees), 4 (left side + layup), 5 (left side), 6 (mid fairway 130â€“150 out), 10 (flat shelf 85 yds out), 12 (left of bunker), 15 (left side landing), 18 (driver landing). Rule: aim at widest part of fairway, driver line.

